# OXR License

Copyright (c) 2026 SoMark Team

OXR is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, subject to the
additional terms below. These additional terms take precedence in the event
of a conflict; otherwise, Apache License 2.0 applies.

## 1. Commercial License and Thresholds

Commercial use of OXR and its Derivative Works is permitted without a
separate commercial license only while you and your Affiliates, on a
consolidated basis, do not exceed either of the following thresholds:

(a) USD 2,000,000 in Total Funding; or
(b) USD 2,000,000 in Annual Revenue.

If either threshold is exceeded, you must obtain a separate commercial
license from SoMark Team before commencing or continuing commercial use.
Being below these thresholds does not waive any other term of this License,
including the competing hosted API restriction in Section 3.

## 2. Online Service Attribution

When providing an online service to third parties using OXR or its Derivative
Works, you must prominently identify SoMark OXR in the service's user interface or
publicly accessible documentation.

## 3. Competing Hosted API Services

Unless expressly authorized in advance by a separate written license from
SoMark Team, you may not use OXR or its Derivative Works to offer, operate,
or make available to third parties a hosted API service that competes with
a hosted API service offered by SoMark Team or its Affiliates.

This restriction includes services offered through a reseller, a white-label
arrangement, or an intermediary interface, whether paid or free. A competing
hosted API service is one whose principal functionality provides document
parsing, optical character recognition (OCR), document layout analysis, or
document content extraction as a substitute for substantially similar
functionality of a hosted API service offered by SoMark Team or its Affiliates.

This restriction applies regardless of Total Funding or Annual Revenue.
Use solely within your organization and its Affiliates, without offering such
a service to third parties, is not prohibited by this Section; all other
terms of this License still apply.

## 4. Termination

Your rights under this License terminate automatically, without notice from
SoMark Team, if you fail to obtain a commercial license as required by
Section 1, fail to comply with Section 2, or violate Section 3.

## 5. Definitions and Scope

"Affiliates" are entities that directly or indirectly control you, are
controlled by you, or share common control with you. "Control" means the
power to direct an entity's management or operations through ownership,
voting rights, contractual rights, or other means.

"Total Funding" means cumulative equity and debt financing raised from all
sources by you and your Affiliates, on a consolidated basis, excluding
intra-group transactions to avoid double counting.

"Annual Revenue" means the gross revenue of you and your Affiliates for the
most recently completed fiscal year, on a consolidated basis, excluding
intra-group transactions to avoid double counting. Amounts in other
currencies are measured at their US dollar equivalent.

"Derivative Works" has the meaning given in Apache License 2.0. When
redistributing OXR or its Derivative Works, you must include these additional
terms together with Apache License 2.0. Third-party components separately
identified as being under other licenses remain governed by those licenses.

The full text of Apache License 2.0 is available at
https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0 .

